{"title":"Career Roadmap · Religious Educator","role":"Religious Educator","summary":"A Religious Educator teaches and facilitates learning about religious traditions, sacred texts, ethics, history, theology, philosophy, culture and religious practices. Depending on the institution, the role may involve children, youth, adults, community groups, schools, seminaries, colleges or faith-based organisations.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Theology / Religious Studies"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["The career combines theological/religious knowledge","pedagogy","communication","pastoral sensitivity","curriculum development."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Typical route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Theology/Religious Studies","Teaching/Community Internship","Religious Education Assistant","Religious Educator","Senior Educator","Programme/Curriculum Lead","Religious Education Director"]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Requirements differ substantially between secular academic roles, faith-community education and regulated school-teaching positions. Some religious institutions may also require denomination-specific theological formation, ministerial training or formal authorisation. Verify the requirements of the specific institution and tradition."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2027"},{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Theology/religious studies + communication"}],[{"text":"2027–2028"},{"text":"Skill Building"},{"text":"Pedagogy + curriculum development"}],[{"text":"2028–2029"},{"text":"Professional Preparation"},{"text":"Teaching/community experience"}],[{"text":"2029–2031"},{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Religious Education Assistant / Educator"}],[{"text":"2031–2034"},{"text":"Development"},{"text":"Senior Religious Educator"}],[{"text":"2034–2038"},{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Curriculum / Youth / Adult Education"}],[{"text":"2038–2042"},{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Programme/Curriculum Manager"}],[{"text":"2042–2046"},{"text":"Senior Leadership"},{"text":"Religious Education Director / Academic Leader"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Religious Studies Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a strong understanding of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Theology / Religious Studies"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the programme and tradition:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sacred texts"},{"text":"Theology"},{"text":"Religious history"},{"text":"Religious philosophy"},{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Comparative religion"},{"text":"Religious traditions"},{"text":"Rituals and practices"},{"text":"Religious institutions"},{"text":"Religion and society"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Academic Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Critical reading"},{"text":"Textual analysis"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Public speaking"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Discussion facilitation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important Professional Skill"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to distinguish between:"},{"type":"p","text":"Describing a religious tradition academically and teaching within a particular faith tradition."},{"type":"p","text":"A professional educator should present beliefs, interpretations and historical claims accurately and respectfully."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Pedagogy + Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Educational psychology"},{"text":"Learning theories"},{"text":"Lesson planning"},{"text":"Classroom management"},{"text":"Group facilitation"},{"text":"Age-appropriate communication"},{"text":"Discussion techniques"},{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Question design"},{"text":"Assessment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Learn to Teach Different Audiences"},{"type":"p","text":"A lesson for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Children"},{"text":"Teenagers"},{"text":"University students"},{"text":"Adults"},{"text":"Community groups"}]},{"type":"p","text":"should not use the same teaching method."},{"type":"h","text":"Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"10 lesson plans"},{"text":"5 discussion guides"},{"text":"5 educational presentations"},{"text":"5 short educational videos"},{"text":"3 age-specific teaching modules"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Curriculum + Community Education"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Curriculum design"},{"text":"Religious literacy"},{"text":"Comparative religion"},{"text":"Interfaith understanding"},{"text":"Ethics education"},{"text":"Cultural sensitivity"},{"text":"Community education"},{"text":"Youth engagement"},{"text":"Adult learning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Education"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Presentation design"},{"text":"Learning Management Systems"},{"text":"Online classroom tools"},{"text":"Video production"},{"text":"Digital assessment"},{"text":"Online discussion facilitation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Create a complete:"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Introduction to World Religions\" educational programme"},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Learning objectives"},{"text":"Modules"},{"text":"Readings"},{"text":"Activities"},{"text":"Discussion questions"},{"text":"Assessments"},{"text":"Digital resources"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Professional Religious Education"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to independently design and deliver educational programmes."},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Teaching practice"},{"text":"Curriculum evaluation"},{"text":"Learner assessment"},{"text":"Group facilitation"},{"text":"Parent/community communication"},{"text":"Youth education"},{"text":"Adult education"},{"text":"Educational administration"},{"text":"Safeguarding"},{"text":"Professional boundaries"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Graduation Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Aim for:"},{"type":"flow","items":["20+ lesson plans","5 complete teaching modules","3 educational workshops","2 community projects","teaching/practicum experience"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"School Religious Education"},{"text":"Children and adolescents"}],[{"text":"Youth Religious Education"},{"text":"Teenagers and young adults"}],[{"text":"Adult Religious Education"},{"text":"Adult learners"}],[{"text":"Theology Education"},{"text":"Structured theological learning"}],[{"text":"Sacred Text Education"},{"text":"Textual and interpretive studies"}],[{"text":"Comparative Religion"},{"text":"Multiple religious traditions"}],[{"text":"Ethics Education"},{"text":"Moral and applied ethics"}],[{"text":"Interfaith Education"},{"text":"Religious literacy and dialogue"}],[{"text":"Community Education"},{"text":"Faith/community programmes"}],[{"text":"Digital Religious Education"},{"text":"Online learning"}],[{"text":"Curriculum Development"},{"text":"Educational programme design"}],[{"text":"Religious Education Research"},{"text":"Academic research"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong internship environments include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Schools"},{"text":"Colleges"},{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Religious educational institutions"},{"text":"Seminaries/theological institutions"},{"text":"Community organisations"},{"text":"Youth organisations"},{"text":"Faith-based NGOs"},{"text":"Cultural organisations"},{"text":"Interfaith organisations"},{"text":"Educational foundations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Activities"},{"type":"p","text":"Gain experience in:"},{"type":"